1
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:19,097
Just ten more minutes.

2
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:22,540
Maybe five. Wake up! Now!

3
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:28,710
Sugu?

4
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:37,640
Would you get up already?

5
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,220
It's 5.30.

6
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:42,858
Even though you're a lost
child to Vecta and a guest,

7
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:45,413
you're still expected to get up on time.

8
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:47,910
Okay.

9
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:47,380
SHINING SOME MY DIAMOND!

10
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:30,260
Forty-five!

11
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:38,161
There's a lot I don't
understand about this place.

12
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:41,860
But I know I'm gonna need
Eugeo's help to get to Senator.

13
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:46,200
The thing is, I have to get
him out of his calling first.

14
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:49,621
And to do that, we'll have
to chop this tree down.

15
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:52,720
What was that? Huh? Oh, nothing.

16
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:55,117
We're all done with the morning's quota.

17
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:56,376
It's time for lunch.

18
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,320
I'm starving.

19
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:04,120
You know what I wish?

20
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:07,182
I wish you could have
tasted the pies Alice made.

21
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,678
The crust was so flaky and
there was so much filling.

22
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:13,948
Having it with some
fresh milk was the best.

23
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:17,452
There's nothing in the world
that tasted better than that.

24
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,620
Was that Alice's calling? A baker?

25
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:22,000
No, not even.

26
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:25,877
Back in those days, she was studying
the sacred arts at the church.

27
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,960
She was the greatest prodigy
this village ever had.

28
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:32,177
She could cast all kinds of
spells by the time she was ten.

29
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:33,090
Wow.

30
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:36,617
What's up with the girl
living at the church?

31
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:37,820
You know, Selka?

32
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:40,580
Oh, she's Alice's little sister.

33
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,660
After Alice was taken away,

34
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:47,160
Selka moved to the church to become
a nun and study the sacred arts.

35
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,597
There's a bunch of kids there, too.

36
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:52,897
Are they there for the same reason as her?

37
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:57,137
They lost their parents to the plague
that hit the village three years ago.

38
00:03:57,220 --> 00:04:00,980
The church is the only place that
had room for them. Poor kids.

39
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:03,133
It's like we're cursed.

40
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:06,497
All these strange things
have been happening lately.

41
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:09,777
Like people being attacked and
kidnapped down the main road.

42
00:04:09,860 --> 00:04:12,684
The villagers say goblins
are the ones doing it.

43
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:14,175
There's goblins here?

44
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:16,947
I have a feeling all
that talk's just rumors.

45
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:22,202
If it were true, an Integrity Knight should
have come by now to put a stop to them.

46
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:24,481
They'd have been here in a flash.

47
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:28,077
Like when Alice touched the
ground in the Dark Territory.

48
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:30,480
That was nothing compared to goblins.

49
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,100
No, it's not.

50
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:33,450
Either way,

51
00:04:33,533 --> 00:04:38,057
there have been a lot of deaths over the
past two or three years, more than usual.

52
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:39,434
Can't you revive them?

53
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:42,189
You know, like with
one of the sacred arts?

54
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,680
Well, I don't know about that,

55
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:48,577
but I remember Alice saying
there was a high-level

56
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:51,297
sacred art that could stop
a life from decreasing.

57
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:55,140
That'd be a good one to
know, I guess. It would.

58
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,477
Alice said she found a passage about that

59
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,148
spell in one of the old
books in the church.

60
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:04,456
But the problem is only the high
priest at the Axiom Church can use it.

61
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:05,410
Axiom Church?

62
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:06,880
It's in Senator.

63
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:08,788
They wrote the Taboo Index.

64
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:12,217
But, like, do you have to be a
high priest to use the spell?

65
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:14,888
Maybe someone like you
or me could learn it.

66
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:19,460
No, it's not for regular folk like us.

67
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:22,317
The arts get their strength
from the sacred power

68
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:25,635
that Solus and Terraria
saturate the air and land with.

69
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:29,891
The more elaborate the art,
the more sacred power it takes.

70
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:32,977
It would take more power
than this forest has,

71
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:35,825
and no one from here to
Zakaria could wield it.

72
00:05:37,180 --> 00:05:38,140
That's too bad.

73
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:43,051
I wonder if there's a sacred art that
could help us to chop this thing down.

74
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,165
That would make things easier.

75
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:49,008
There's gotta be something
better than this.

76
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:55,125
Hey, Eugeo, is there anything
tougher than this in your village?

77
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:56,578
No, I'm afraid not.

78
00:05:56,780 --> 00:06:01,192
The only thing stronger than the Dragon
Bone Axe would be an Integrity Ni -

79
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,420
On second thought, maybe there is.

80
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:07,360
Wait here for me.

81
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,160
I'll be back in a bit. Huh?

82
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:21,060
Whoa! You okay?

83
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,740
Mind if I open it?

84
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:28,910
Okay.

85
00:06:28,993 --> 00:06:29,823
Just be careful.

86
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:34,061
If it falls on your foot, it'll
leave you with more than a scratch.

87
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:52,180
No way.

88
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:55,837
Hey, it's the blue rose
sword from the fairy tale.

89
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,100
What fairy tale?

90
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:58,660
It goes like this.

91
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:02,877
300 years ago, Bercouli the
swordsman went to the End Mountains.

92
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:07,740
He entered the lair of the white dragon,
our protector, and found that sword.

93
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:10,540
It's just a silly story.

94
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:16,220
That is, it was, until some kids
decided to find out if it was true.

95
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:18,180
I mentioned it yesterday.

96
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:19,890
Remember?

97
00:07:19,973 --> 00:07:22,657
About how Alice and I
went to the End Mountains?

98
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:25,160
I found that sword in the dragon's lair.

99
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:28,920
I couldn't even lift it by
myself back then. Really?

100
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:32,577
What'd the dragon have to say about
you guys breaking into its home?

101
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:35,457
Oh, there was nothing left
of it except some bones.

102
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:39,834
We took the wrong tunnel, and then
Alice crossed into the Dark Territory.

103
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:44,160
And then she was taken away.

104
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:47,940
I couldn't do anything for
her except stand there.

105
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:52,640
I wanted to save her, but my
arms and legs were frozen.

106
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:54,560
I'm sorry.

107
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:56,039
Back to the sword.

108
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:59,460
I left it there that
day and never forgot it.

109
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:01,680
So two summers ago, I went back.

110
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,120
Every day of rest, I'd go drag it.

111
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:06,557
It took three months to get it back here.

112
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:08,993
It took you three whole months to do it?

113
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,074
Why'd you even bother?

114
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:15,366
I guess I was hoping one day I'd
have the strength to swing it.

115
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,304
I'm still not strong enough to.

116
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:19,397
Do you think you are?

117
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,620
I'm down to try.

118
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,468
I'm a swordsman, after all.

119
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,294
Looks like it's too heavy for you, too.

120
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:39,900
It's not made of steel, or is it?

121
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:41,640
No, I don't think so.

122
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:44,369
And it's not silver or
dragon bone, either.

123
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:47,580
I think it might be a
divine object. A what?

124
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:50,357
It's something that was either made with

125
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:53,160
the help of the gods
or was created by them.

126
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:56,680
We call things like that divine objects.

127
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:57,920
That makes sense.

128
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:02,715
Hey, Eugeo, could you, like, check
how much life the Giga Cedar has now?

129
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:03,650
Don't tell me.

130
00:09:03,733 --> 00:09:04,563
Let me guess.

131
00:09:04,646 --> 00:09:06,937
You're going to try
striking it with the sword.

132
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:08,608
You're damn straight, I am.

133
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:10,857
Unless the Taboo Index forbids it.

134
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:12,705
But I bet it doesn't, does it?

135
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:15,180
No, it doesn't. It's funny.

136
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,068
All this seems so familiar.

137
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:21,970
Hmm.

138
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:26,980
Right now, it's at 232,315. Cool.

139
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:28,200
Remember that.

140
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:49,580
Did you hurt yourself?

141
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:51,880
No, I'm okay.

142
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:54,660
I told you before, that tree is tough.

143
00:09:57,460 --> 00:09:58,540
No way.

144
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,900
You actually cut into it.

145
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:07,160
And deep, too. Go on.

146
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,140
See where its life's at now.

147
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:10,490
Oh, right.

148
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,000
232-3-14.

149
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:16,500
You're kidding.

150
00:10:17,020 --> 00:10:18,820
It only went down one point?

151
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,420
Your hit landed in the wrong spot.

152
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,617
I bet it would have decreased
its life a lot more if

153
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:27,994
you got it in the center of
the cut instead of the bark.

154
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:30,197
Looks like your intuition was right.

155
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:32,692
The sword is more effective than the axe.

156
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:36,520
Even so, we'd have to master
using it to get any results.

157
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:39,467
I can't hit it straight,
but I bet you could.

158
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:42,544
I can barely hold the
sword, let alone swing it.

159
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:45,955
It's all about technique,
and I can help you with that.

160
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,190
Mm.

161
00:10:48,273 --> 00:10:49,329
Okay, I'll give it a shot.

162
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:57,200
It's so heavy.

163
00:10:57,540 --> 00:10:59,057
First thing, find your balance.

164
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:00,877
And when you swing, swing with your body.

165
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:04,117
With swords, it's more about
momentum, not just arm strength.

166
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,030
Mm-hmm.

167
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:27,900
Hey, you all right?

168
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:30,460
I think I lost some life on that one.

169
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:32,900
Oh, well, it was a good try.

170
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:45,916
If durability's life, I lost
some when I took a swing.

171
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:47,850
Hmm.

172
00:11:47,933 --> 00:11:50,140
It says my object control
authority's at 38.

173
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,147
I guess that's my parameter.

174
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:57,960
The sword's is higher.

175
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,525
That's what I'm talking about.

176
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,420
At this rate, I'll never get to Senator.

177
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:14,120
I need Eugeo's help, but he
won't bail on his calling.

178
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:18,777
If it wasn't for that taboo
index he could do whatever

179
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:22,637
he wants he said the axiom
church came up with it.

180
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:24,797
Wonder what the deal is with them?

181
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:29,157
If I'm right and these people
are ai flux lights in a simulated

182
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:33,340
civilization there's no way the
system would let him break a rule.

183
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:38,857
Hang on Eiji said Alice broke the taboo

184
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:40,997
index when she accidentally
crossed into the

185
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:45,777
dark territory but she
was there by choice she

186
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:49,957
went against the system
so is she not an ai?

187
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:50,880
Hello

188
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,350
is someone in there?

189
00:12:52,433 --> 00:12:55,437
Yeah there is I'm almost done.

190
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:59,897
Oh um no you can take your
time I was just checking.

191
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:02,077
Sorry to bother you. Good night.

192
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:05,740
Uh Selka I wanted to ask you something.

193
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:20,380
So, what was it you
wanted to ask me? Yeah.

194
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:25,790
Um...

195
00:13:26,940 --> 00:13:28,646
It's about your older sister.

196
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,320
I heard about her.

197
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:33,060
You know, from Eugeo.

198
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:36,480
And like, he told me her name was Alice.

199
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:37,840
He did, did he?

200
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:41,197
What else did he tell you,
besides her name was Alice?

201
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:45,540
Oh, um, he said she was studying
the sacred arts here at the church.

202
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:49,240
And how six years ago an
Integrity Knight took her.

203
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:52,264
I got the feeling he's
really worried about her.

204
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:53,660
I didn't know.

205
00:13:54,060 --> 00:13:55,960
I thought he forgot about her.

206
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,255
This explains a lot about him, though.

207
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:01,820
She's the reason Eugeo's so sad.

208
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,180
I didn't get that.

209
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:05,420
He seems fine. He's not.

210
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:09,137
You had to have noticed it,
how quiet and gloomy he is.

211
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:10,540
Oh, yeah.

212
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:16,420
When my sister was here, every time I
saw him, he had a smile on his face.

213
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:20,415
I don't remember ever seeing
him without one back then.

214
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:21,980
But not anymore.

215
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:24,937
He spends his days of rest alone,

216
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:28,432
and the only time I see him
is when he goes to the forest.

217
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:32,240
Selka, you really like him, don't you?

218
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:35,700
I didn't see that! Oh my gosh!

219
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:41,357
Everyone compares me to Alice.

220
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,028
No one says it, but I know.

221
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:48,520
When my parents see me, I remind them
of her, and I can't stand it anymore.

222
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:51,720
That's probably why Eugeo avoids me.

223
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:56,480
When he sees me, he thinks of her,
and I can tell it makes him sad.

224
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:59,240
But there's nothing I can do.

225
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:02,200
It's not my fault she's gone.

226
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:07,020
I'm sorry.

227
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:08,780
I'm acting like a baby.

228
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:10,680
No, not at all.

229
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,260
It's good to cry.

230
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:14,424
It's better than holding it in.

231
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:17,600
Yes, you're right.

232
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:20,317
In fact, I feel much better already.

233
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:23,540
Crying in front of others
is not something I do.

234
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:25,410
Really?

235
00:15:25,493 --> 00:15:26,597
You're tougher than I am.

236
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:30,327
I can't tell you how many times
I've cried in front of people.

237
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:32,600
Hold on.

238
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:34,260
Is your memory back?

239
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:37,200
No, it just feels that way is all.

240
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:38,796
Anyway, back to you.

241
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:41,217
It doesn't matter what anyone thinks.

242
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:42,877
You're you, not your sister.

243
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:46,340
You can only live your
life, not someone else's.

244
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:48,679
Yes, you're right.

245
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,660
I should get going.

246
00:15:57,180 --> 00:16:02,004
Say, did Yu-Gi-Oh happen to tell you why
the Integrity Knight took my sister away?

247
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:04,320
Um, yeah, he did.

248
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:08,246
My parents wouldn't tell me, and
Eugeo wouldn't tell me either.

249
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:11,100
Maybe you could tell me why?

250
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:12,300
Yeah, sure.

251
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:17,564
She went to the End Mountains, then touched
the ground on the Dark Territory side.

252
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:19,300
I see.

253
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:21,020
The End Mountains, huh?

254
00:16:24,940 --> 00:16:26,528
Tomorrow's our day of rest.

255
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:27,777
Still, be on time.

256
00:16:27,860 --> 00:16:29,897
I won't be coming to wake you up anymore.

257
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:32,120
Okay, I'll keep that in mind.

258
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,780
Good morning.

259
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,900
Oh, good morning. By chance.

260
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,600
Have you seen Selka today? No.

261
00:16:56,900 --> 00:16:58,371
I just woke up, actually.

262
00:16:58,840 --> 00:16:59,670
So I see.

263
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:02,255
Well, I have not seen her all morning.

264
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:05,480
She missed prayers, and
she is not in her room.

265
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:09,560
I am worried she would never
leave without telling me first.

266
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:11,074
I'm sure she's around.

267
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:12,260
I hope so.

268
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:15,580
If you see her, please
let me know. Yes, ma 'am.

269
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:19,880
Yujiro! Hey, Kirito!

270
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:21,877
Have you seen Selka anywhere?

271
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,440
I haven't. Why?

272
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,136
Sister Azalea's been looking for her.

273
00:17:26,520 --> 00:17:28,597
She says she left without telling her.

274
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:29,562
That's strange.

275
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:31,297
Well, I'm trying to find her.

276
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:32,877
Do you know where she could have gone?

277
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:35,220
No, she and I haven't spoken in ages.

278
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:38,368
Do you think something
might have upset her?

279
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:41,100
I see.

280
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:42,880
The End Mountains, huh?

281
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:47,277
Man, last night I told her
what happened to Alice.

282
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:50,066
At least everything you
told me that happened.

283
00:17:50,980 --> 00:17:54,451
She wouldn't go to the End
Mountains on her own, would she?

284
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:56,517
That's exactly where she went.

285
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:58,365
We have to bring her back now.

286
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:07,270
What's wrong?

287
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,275
It's been stepped on.

288
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:14,172
It's lost a bit of life.

289
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:17,817
Someone's been by here, and
it wasn't that long ago.

290
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:19,317
Then we're on the right track.

291
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:20,697
That's got to be Selka.

292
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:21,610
Yeah.

293
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:28,140
Well, this is it.

294
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:30,880
No way.

295
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:33,060
It really is the end.

296
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:36,660
When I first came here,
I thought the same thing.

297
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:41,320
And the dark territory's
down that way, huh? Yeah.

298
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:42,560
Are you ready?

299
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:44,740
Yeah, I think. I guess.

300
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:46,220
System call.

301
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:49,060
Generate luminous elements.

302
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:50,570
Adhere.

303
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:54,060
Eugeo, what'd you do?

304
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:55,620
It's a sacred art.

305
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:57,642
An easy one that anybody can do.

306
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:59,660
But, like, you said system.

307
00:18:59,860 --> 00:19:01,417
Do you even know what that means?

308
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:02,330
Nothing.

309
00:19:02,413 --> 00:19:03,243
It's just a word.

310
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:04,401
Well, a command.

311
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,351
It's to call on the gods.

312
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:10,177
As long as you have enough skill, you'll
be blessed with the art you summon.

313
00:19:10,260 --> 00:19:12,600
He thinks he's casting a magic spell.

314
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:15,640
Come on. Let's go. Right.

315
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:25,200
Maybe she didn't come in here.

316
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:27,384
I mean, there's no sign of her.

317
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:33,280
This is as good a sign as any.

318
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:35,280
It could be her, I guess.

319
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:41,337
Hey, Yujiya. What is it?

320
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:43,980
If she crosses into the Dark Territory,

321
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:47,177
does an Integrity Knight
come and take her right away?

322
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:49,220
No, not until the next day.

323
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:54,016
He'll fly to the village and arrest
her there, just like six years ago.

324
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:59,184
Then, even if we're too late, we still
have a chance to keep him from getting her.

325
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:02,760
But that would be interfering. We can't.

326
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:04,460
Of course we can.

327
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:07,547
Look, even if she does
break the taboo index,

328
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:09,797
all we have to do is keep
her away from the village.

329
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:13,351
The Integrity Knight can't
arrest her if he can't find her.

330
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:14,540
That's insane.

331
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:16,760
We can't hide forever.

332
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:18,600
And I have my calling.

333
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:20,938
But I don't, so I can take her away.

334
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:25,257
If I didn't say anything,
she wouldn't be in this mess.

335
00:20:25,340 --> 00:20:26,399
This is all on me.

336
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:28,260
No, it's not.

337
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:31,090
Sugou!

338
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:35,830
That way!

339
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:43,800
Take cover!

340
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:00,710
Crap!

341
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:01,700
Goblins!

342
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:12,300
Sugou!

343
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:13,838
What are you doing?

344
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:23,240
Looky looky!

345
00:21:23,480 --> 00:21:28,160
Two more white Eum brassy brats
just a-wondering around! Yummy!

346
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:30,424
Let's tie him to the other one!

347
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:33,160
Silence!

348
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:36,060
They're male Eums!

349
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:40,120
We take them back, no
one buy them. Worthless.

350
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:42,620
Kill them and make them meat instead.

351
00:21:45,560 --> 00:22:02,430
Eugeo!

352
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:07,117
Love you,

353
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:13,337
Love you, Love you!

354
00:22:24,020 --> 00:22:27,820
I will see the bright green flowers.

355
00:22:28,300 --> 00:22:33,300
The breeze will show the sky
that looks so bright as the sky.

356
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:03,424
Thank you so much for watching.

357
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:38,100
Next time, Departure.
